# Line endings
#
# This repo is worked on from Windows, but its scripts are executed by
# Linux/macOS harnesses — a `.sh` file that reaches disk with CRLF fails on
# the shebang line with `$'\r': command not found`, which is what happened to
# the synced copy of repo-config's audit.sh.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the WORKING TREE on every platform, not just in the
# index, so a Windows checkout produces the same bytes a Linux one does and
# anything copying files out of that checkout (skill sync, install_skills.py,
# build_skill_zips.py) carries LF with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the two file types that actually execute.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Skill archives are zip files. Git already detects these as binary, but say
# so explicitly so `text=auto` above can never guess wrong on one.
*.skill binary
*.zip binary
